CSS:
======
cascading style sheets
cascading --> flowing
styles --> properties
sheets --> doc
-->css means used to describe the presentation of a html document and it deals with colors,text,fonts,backgrounds,animations,layouts and media queries

HOW TO INSERT CSS:
==================
1)INLINE CSS : styles are added to the html element itself by using style attribute <h1 style = 'color:red;'>inline content</h1>
2)INTERNAL CSS : styles are added to the html document using style tag in head section 
  <style>
    </style>
  SELECTORS : used to target the html elements for applying styles
  syntax : selector{
          declaration
          property : value;
          }

        eg: h2
           {color:green;
           }
3)EXTERNAL CSS : styles are defined in external file that has .css extension

HIGH SPECIFICITY : high precedence
inline having high SPECIFICITY
based on how we define - preferred internal then external 

TYPES OF SELECTORS:
===================
1) simple SELECTORS:
=======================
  a)element selector or tagname selector : styles will be applied based on a element
     h1{
        color:red;
     }
  b) class selector : used to apply styles to the multiple elements
      .title{
          color:green;
           }
        <h1 class ="title title2">inline content</h1>
        <h2 class ="title">internal content</h2>
        <h3 class ="title">external content</h3>

        -->can take multiple class names
        .title1{
            color:green;
             }
        .title2{
                color:yellow;
            }

  c)id selector : denoted by #idname  
      #colors{
        color : blue;
      }

specificity in selectors:
===========================
1)id having high specificity
2)class having medium specificity
3)tagname having low specificity

